  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Offerpad’s revenue contracted sharply as the company deliberately scaled back home acquisitions and sales, shifting toward a smaller, more selective pipeline in a cautious housing environment. Despite deeply lower transaction volumes, per-home economics strengthened meaningfully — gross profit per sale and contribution after interest both improved — reflecting tighter underwriting and operational discipline. The firm is leaning on its multi-solution platform and AI-driven tools to lift engagement and conversion, prioritizing transaction efficiency over volume-driven growth.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is firmly focused on the path to profitability, having slashed operating expenses and narrowed adjusted EBITDA losses sequentially while reiterating a target of positive EBITDA before year-end. Although revenue missed expectations and near-term guidance came in well below consensus, management’s cost discipline, improved liquidity, and reduced leverage underscore a deliberate shift to a leaner, self-sustaining model. The sharp top-line pullback and conservative outlook have nonetheless tested market confidence, tempering enthusiasm about how quickly a return to growth can materialize.",
